Empyema,"An empyema () is a collection or gathering of pus within a naturally existing anatomical cavity. For example, pleural empyema is empyema of the pleural cavity. It must be differentiated from an abscess, which is a collection of pus in a newly formed cavity. The term is from Greek ¼ÀÍ·¼±, ""abscess"".

Classification
Empyema occurs in:

the pleural cavity (pleural empyema also known as pyothorax)
the thoracic cavity
the uterus (pyometra)
the appendix (appendicitis)
the meninges (subdural empyema)
the joints (septic arthritis)
the gallbladder

